From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thibaut Lapierre <root@epheo.eu>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:35:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] ovn: enable network segmentation

UserDefinedNetwork and ClusterUserDefinedNetwork served, primary networks
included, as on OpenShift: enable-network-segmentation and
enable-preconfigured-udn-addresses in ovnkube.conf, --enable-persistent-ips
on the cluster manager (OpenShift passes it there alone), the UDN, CUDN
and IPAMClaim CRDs in MicroShift's CRD list so they exist before OVN-K
starts, and the cluster manager's rights to render NADs and own the
networks' status. A project gets its own primary network, isolated by
construction; VMs keep their addresses through IPAMClaims. Needs 0001.

udn-allowed-default-services names MicroShift's DNS Service: OVN-K's
default, kube-system/kube-dns, does not exist here, and pods on a primary
UDN would resolve nothing. dns-service-namespace and dns-service-name give
the same Service to the DHCP OVN-K serves VMs on a primary layer2 network.

The CRD files are not carried: the SRPM stage writes them from the
payload's cluster-network-operator (src/image/payload-crds.sh). The
namespace-label admission policy and the UDN user roles come from the same
operator through src/rbac/vendor.sh.

Upstream: no config knob as of 5.0.
Covered by: vm-test (two primary CUDNs isolate their namespaces from each
other and from the default network, each still reaches DNS and the API, an
IPAMClaim keeps a pod's address across a recreate) and multinode-test (a
primary CUDN spans nodes).
---
 .../ovn/common/clusterrole-controller.yaml    | 46 +++++++++++++++++++
 assets/components/ovn/common/configmap.yaml   |  5 ++
 .../ovn/single-node/master/daemonset.yaml     |  3 +-
 .../ovn/zones/master/daemonset.yaml           |  3 +-
 pkg/assets/crd.go                             |  3 ++
 5 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/assets/components/ovn/common/clusterrole-controller.yaml b/assets/components/ovn/common/clusterrole-controller.yaml
index 8aaa4e18682cacd85e3abbbcca12f768906df4af..670012aaba049d37cb0ab1308443c2b9821cdcf6 100644
--- a/assets/components/ovn/common/clusterrole-controller.yaml
+++ b/assets/components/ovn/common/clusterrole-controller.yaml
@@ -177,3 +177,49 @@ rules:
   - egressfirewalls/status
   verbs:
   - patch
+# enable-network-segmentation: the cluster manager renders each UDN and CUDN
+# into NADs in the namespaces it selects, deletes them with the network, and
+# owns the networks' status and finalizers. Same crash loop when forbidden.
+- apiGroups: ["k8s.ovn.org"]
+  resources:
+  - userdefinednetworks
+  - clusteruserdefinednetworks
+  verbs:
+  - get
+  - list
+  - watch
+  - patch
+  - update
+- apiGroups: ["k8s.ovn.org"]
+  resources:
+  - userdefinednetworks/status
+  - clusteruserdefinednetworks/status
+  verbs:
+  - patch
+  - update
+- apiGroups: ["k8s.ovn.org"]
+  resources:
+  - userdefinednetworks/finalizers
+  - clusteruserdefinednetworks/finalizers
+  verbs:
+  - update
+- apiGroups: ["k8s.cni.cncf.io"]
+  resources:
+  - network-attachment-definitions
+  verbs:
+  - delete
+# --enable-persistent-ips: the cluster manager records each claimed address
+# in the IPAMClaim's status, so a VM keeps it across restarts and migrations.
+- apiGroups: ["k8s.cni.cncf.io"]
+  resources:
+  - ipamclaims
+  verbs:
+  - get
+  - list
+  - watch
+- apiGroups: ["k8s.cni.cncf.io"]
+  resources:
+  - ipamclaims/status
+  verbs:
+  - patch
+  - update
diff --git a/assets/components/ovn/common/configmap.yaml b/assets/components/ovn/common/configmap.yaml
index 0c7a9334f3ab2cca71f359b0d0b524d3301963ed..299fef47628b3930d9c27f2489d2476222113e9d 100644
